<Content
  kicker="Legal"
  title="Tokens & Wallet"
  description="What avaTOK tokens are, how top-ups convert into tokens, what they can be spent on, and what happens to a balance."
  lead="Tokens are the in-app unit you use to pay for AI features and services on avaTOK."
  updated="2026-08-05"
>
  <p>
    This page explains how tokens and the in-app wallet work on avaTOK. It sits alongside our
    <a href="/terms">Terms of Service</a>, <a href="/refunds">Refunds &amp; Cancellations</a>
    policy, <a href="/payouts">Payouts &amp; Withdrawals</a> policy, and
    <a href="/pricing-fees">Pricing &amp; Fees</a> page.
  </p>

  <h2>1. Who you are dealing with</h2>
  <p>
    Which company holds your balance depends on where you are:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Ava Global International Pvt Ltd</strong>, Mumbai, India — contracts with and serves
      customers in India, and handles India transactions and payouts under Indian law and GST.</li>
    <li><strong>Ava Global International, Inc.</strong>, Delaware, USA — contracts with and serves
      international (non-India) customers, and handles international transactions and payouts.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>2. What a token is</h2>
  <p>
    A token is an in-app unit of account. It records how much service you are entitled to use on
    avaTOK. It exists only inside your avaTOK account and only for use on the platform.
  </p>

  <h2>3. Top-ups convert into tokens</h2>
  <p>
    When you top up — in INR for India, or in USD or another supported currency internationally —
    the amount you pay is converted into tokens and credited to your wallet. The conversion applied
    is the one shown at the time of the top-up. Once converted, the balance is expressed and used in
    tokens, not in currency.
  </p>

  <h2>4. What tokens are not</h2>
  <div class="note">
    <p>
      Tokens have <strong>no independent monetary value outside the avaTOK platform</strong>. They
      are <strong>not</strong> a deposit, not a bank balance, not e-money or a payment instrument,
      not a security or investment, and not a cryptocurrency or virtual digital asset. They do not
      earn interest, they are not transferable to another person, and they carry no ownership or
      profit rights in either company.
    </p>
  </div>

  <h2>5. What tokens can be spent on</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>AI features</strong> inside the app.</li>
    <li><strong>Marketplace purchases</strong> — digital services offered by other users.</li>
    <li><strong>Consultations</strong> — live consultancy sessions you book on the platform.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    The token cost of a feature or service is shown before you confirm. Costs may change over time;
    see <a href="/pricing-fees">Pricing &amp; Fees</a>. Some features may be unavailable in some
    countries, or may be turned off temporarily.
  </p>

  <h2>6. Your balance</h2>
  <p>
    Your current token balance and recent activity are shown in the app. Please check your balance
    and transaction history regularly and tell us promptly if something looks wrong.
  </p>

  <h2>7. Correcting balance errors</h2>
  <p>
    We may adjust a balance to correct a technical error, a duplicate credit, a failed or reversed
    payment, a chargeback, or credit issued in error or obtained through abuse of a promotion. Where
    we make an adjustment, we will normally record it in your transaction history. If you disagree
    with an adjustment, contact <a href="mailto:support@avatok.ai">support@avatok.ai</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>8. Withdrawing unused tokens</h2>
  <p>
    Unused tokens may be withdrawn, subject to verification and to the fee and any tax shown at the
    time of withdrawal. India payouts go to a verified UPI address linked to your Indian bank
    account; international payouts are handled by the US entity. The full rules are on the
    <a href="/payouts">Payouts &amp; Withdrawals</a> page.
  </p>
  <p>
    Tokens already spent are consumed and cannot be withdrawn. Refund rules are set out in
    <a href="/refunds">Refunds &amp; Cancellations</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>9. Suspension and account closure</h2>
  <p>
    If your account is suspended — for example while we investigate suspected fraud, a chargeback,
    or a breach of our <a href="/terms">Terms of Service</a> — we may temporarily prevent you from
    spending or withdrawing your balance while the matter is reviewed.
  </p>
  <p>
    If you close your account, or if we terminate it, you may ask us to withdraw any remaining
    unused balance, subject to verification, the applicable fee, any tax, and any amount we are
    entitled to set off or are required by law to withhold. We may decline to release a balance
    where doing so would be unlawful, or where the balance is linked to fraud or to a breach of our
    Terms.
  </p>

  <h2>10. Expiry</h2>
  <p>
    Tokens do not carry an expiry date under this policy. If that ever changes, we will say so here
    and give notice in the app before it takes effect.
  </p>

  <h2>11. Changes to this policy</h2>
  <p>
    We may update this policy from time to time. We will post the updated version here and revise
    the "Last updated" date above.
  </p>

  <h2>12. Contact</h2>
  <p>
    Wallet, billing, and payout questions:
    <a href="mailto:support@avatok.ai">support@avatok.ai</a>. General enquiries:
    <a href="mailto:hello@avatok.ai">hello@avatok.ai</a>. See also our
    <a href="/terms">Terms of Service</a> and <a href="/privacy">Privacy Policy</a>.
  </p>
</Content>
